---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro'
import JsonLd from '../components/JsonLd.astro'
import SourceLinks from '../components/SourceLinks.astro'
import { SITE } from '../lib/site.js'
import { SRC } from '../lib/sources.js'

const agent = SITE.agentName
const brokerage = SITE.brokerage
const area = SITE.areaSentence

// Each step is written so it still makes sense if read on its own.
const steps = [
  {
    title: 'Get your finances in order',
    body: 'Before you buy a home, check your credit, decide on a monthly payment you are comfortable with, and plan for a down payment and closing costs. A mortgage lender can review your numbers and tell you what you qualify for.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Get pre-approved',
    body: 'A pre-approval is a letter from a mortgage lender saying how much they are likely to lend you. It shows sellers you are a serious buyer and sets your price range before you start touring homes.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Search and tour homes',
    body: `List your must-haves and nice-to-haves for a home, then tour homes with ${agent}, who points out what to look for beyond the staging.`,
  },
  {
    title: 'Make an offer',
    body: `Once you find a home, ${agent} uses comparable sales (recent sales of similar nearby homes) to help you choose a price and terms that are competitive without overpaying.`,
  },
  {
    title: 'Inspection and appraisal',
    body: `After the seller accepts your offer, a home inspection and the lender’s appraisal check the home’s condition and value. You can negotiate repairs based on what the inspection finds.`,
  },
  {
    title: 'Close and get your keys',
    body: 'At closing, you sign the final paperwork at the title company and bring your closing funds. After that, the home is yours and you get the keys.',
  },
]

// Minimum down payment by loan type, shown as a table inside the down payment FAQ.
const downPaymentRows = [
  {
    loan: 'Conventional',
    down: 'As low as 3% for eligible buyers (20% avoids mortgage insurance)',
    note: 'Mortgage insurance is typically required with less than 20% down',
  },
  {
    loan: 'FHA',
    down: '3.5%',
    note: 'HUD says FHA loans are a good option for first-time buyers',
  },
  {
    loan: 'VA',
    down: '0%',
    note: 'For eligible veterans and service members',
  },
  {
    loan: 'USDA',
    down: '0%',
    note: 'For eligible homes in qualifying rural areas',
  },
]

// Each answer is a list of blocks: { text, lead? }, { table: true }, or { note: true, text }.
// Every answer names its subject, so it makes sense even if read without the rest of the page.
const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'How do I buy my first home in Idaho Falls?',
    blocks: [
      {
        text: `To buy your first home in Idaho Falls, you get your finances in order, get pre-approved with a mortgage lender, search and tour homes, make an offer, complete the home inspection and appraisal, and close. ${agent}, a licensed Idaho real estate agent with ${brokerage}, guides first-time buyers through each step in ${area}.`,
      },
    ],
  },
  {
    q: 'How much do I need for a down payment when buying my first home in Idaho?',
    blocks: [
      { text: 'The down payment depends on the type of loan you choose.' },
      {
        lead: 'Conventional loans:',
        text: `A conventional loan is a mortgage that isn’t backed by the government. The traditional down payment is 20%, which also lets you avoid private mortgage insurance (PMI), an extra monthly cost that protects the lender. Eligible buyers can put down as little as 3% through Fannie Mae’s HomeReady and standard 97% loans and Freddie Mac’s Home Possible. With less than 20% down, mortgage insurance is typically required. Eligibility varies by program. HomeReady requires a credit score of 620, HomeReady and Home Possible limit household income to 80% of the area median, Fannie Mae’s standard 3% down loan needs at least one first-time buyer, and homeownership education can be required when every borrower is a first-time buyer. The home must be a one-unit primary residence.`,
        sources: [SRC.fannieHomeReady, SRC.fannie97, SRC.freddieHomePossible, SRC.cfpbMortgageInsurance],
      },
      {
        lead: 'Other loan options:',
        text: 'FHA loans can start at 3.5% down, and FHA mortgage insurance is required on every FHA loan. VA loans (for eligible veterans and service members) and USDA loans (for eligible homes in qualifying rural areas) can require 0% down.',
        sources: [SRC.hudFha, SRC.cfpbMortgageInsurance, SRC.vaPurchase, SRC.usdaGuaranteed],
      },
      { table: true },
      {
        lead: 'Other costs:',
        text: 'A down payment is only part of the cash you need. You should also plan for closing costs and a home inspection.',
      },
      {
        text: `A mortgage lender can tell you which loan and down payment fit your situation. ${agent} can help you plan the rest of the buying process.`,
      },
      {
        note: true,
        text: `${agent} is not a lender. Loan requirements vary by lender, so confirm the details with a mortgage lender.`,
      },
    ],
  },
  {
    q: 'What are closing costs and the home inspection when buying a home in Idaho?',
    blocks: [
      {
        text: 'Closing costs are the fees you pay to finish the purchase, separate from your down payment. The Consumer Financial Protection Bureau groups them into lender charges, optional points that lower your rate, required third-party services such as the appraisal and title insurance, local government fees, and prepaid items and deposits such as interest, the first year of homeowners insurance, and starting escrow deposits for property taxes and insurance.',
        sources: [SRC.cfpbClosingCosts],
      },
      {
        text: `The home inspection and real estate agent fees are not required by the mortgage, so the CFPB lists them as other homebuying expenses. Your lender must give you a Loan Estimate within three business days of receiving your application, which shows estimated closing costs, the monthly payment, and the interest rate on a standard form, so you can compare lenders side by side. Bring yours to your consultation with ${agent}. Idaho Housing’s down payment assistance can go toward closing costs for eligible buyers.`,
        sources: [SRC.cfpbClosingCosts, SRC.cfpbLoanEstimate, SRC.idahoHousingDpa],
      },
      {
        note: true,
        text: `${agent} is not a lender. Confirm closing cost details with a mortgage lender.`,
      },
    ],
  },
  {
    q: 'Do I need a real estate agent to buy a home, and what does it cost me?',
    blocks: [
      {
        text: `You are not required to use a real estate agent to buy a home, but an agent helps with searching for homes, pricing, negotiation, and keeping contract deadlines on track. ${agent}, a licensed agent with ${brokerage}, explains every step so first-time buyers know what they are signing.`,
      },
      {
        text: `Under rules that took effect August 17, 2024, an agent working with a buyer must have a written agreement with them before touring a home. That agreement has to state the agent’s compensation as a specific amount or rate, and it must say that broker fees and commissions are not set by law and are fully negotiable. The first consultation with ${agent} is free, and he explains how his compensation works on that call, before you agree to anything.`,
        sources: [SRC.narSettlement],
      },
    ],
  },
  {
    q: 'Can I get help before I am ready to buy a home?',
    blocks: [
      {
        text: `Yes. ${agent} offers first-time buyers a free 20 to 30 minute buyer consultation by video call, even if you are months away from buying a home. There is no obligation.`,
      },
    ],
  },
]

// Plain-text version of each answer for the FAQ structured data (tables and links are left out).
const faqSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: faqs.map((item) => ({
    '@type': 'Question',
    name: item.q,
    acceptedAnswer: {
      '@type': 'Answer',
      text: item.blocks
        .filter((b) => b.text)
        .map((b) => (b.lead ? `${b.lead} ${b.text}` : b.text))
        .join(' '),
    },
  })),
}
---

<Layout
  title="First-Time Home Buyer Guide"
  description={`A plain-language guide for first-time home buyers in ${area}: the steps from budget and pre-approval to offer and closing, with local help from ${agent}.`}
>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <JsonLd data={faqSchema} />
  </Fragment>

  <section class="bg-brand py-12 text-center text-white">
    <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-gold">First-Time Buyers</p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 font-heading text-3xl sm:text-4xl">
      Buying Your First Home in Southeast Idaho: The Steps
    </h1>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-16">
    <p class="text-lg text-stone-700">
      To buy your first home in Idaho Falls, you get your finances in order, get pre-approved by a
      lender, tour homes, make an offer, complete the inspection and appraisal, then close and get
      your keys. Here is what each step looks like, so nothing comes as a surprise.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-stone-600">
      {agent} is a licensed Idaho real estate agent with {brokerage}, helping first-time buyers in
      {area} understand the buying process and make confident decisions.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-stone-50 py-16">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6">
      <h2 class="font-heading text-2xl text-brand">{`The ${steps.length} Steps to Buying Your First Home`}</h2>
      <ol class="mt-8 space-y-6">
        {
          steps.map((step, i) => (
            <li class="flex gap-4">
              <span class="flex h-8 w-8 flex-shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-gold font-semibold text-brand-dark">
                {i + 1}
              </span>
              <div>
                <h3 class="font-semibold text-stone-900">{step.title}</h3>
                <p class="mt-1 text-stone-600">{step.body}</p>
              </div>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-16">
    <h2 class="font-heading text-2xl text-brand">
      First-Time Home Buyer Questions in Idaho Falls and Southeast Idaho
    </h2>
    <div class="mt-8 space-y-10">
      {
        faqs.map((item) => (
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-stone-900">{item.q}</h3>
            {item.blocks.map((block) =>
              block.table ? (
                <div class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto">
                  <table class="w-full border-collapse text-left text-sm">
                    <caption class="sr-only">Minimum down payment by loan type</caption>
                    <thead class="bg-stone-100 text-stone-900">
                      <tr>
                        <th scope="col" class="border border-stone-200 px-3 py-2 font-semibold">
                          Loan type
                        </th>
                        <th scope="col" class="border border-stone-200 px-3 py-2 font-semibold">
                          Minimum down payment
                        </th>
                        <th scope="col" class="border border-stone-200 px-3 py-2 font-semibold">
                          Good to know
                        </th>
                      </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody class="text-stone-600">
                      {downPaymentRows.map((row) => (
                        <tr>
                          <th scope="row" class="border border-stone-200 px-3 py-2 font-medium text-stone-900">
                            {row.loan}
                          </th>
                          <td class="border border-stone-200 px-3 py-2">{row.down}</td>
                          <td class="border border-stone-200 px-3 py-2">{row.note}</td>
                        </tr>
                      ))}
                    </tbody>
                  </table>
                </div>
              ) : block.note ? (
                <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-stone-500">{block.text}</p>
              ) : (
                <Fragment>
                  <p class="mt-3 text-stone-600">
                    {block.lead && <strong class="font-semibold text-stone-900">{block.lead} </strong>}
                    {block.text}
                  </p>
                  {block.sources && <SourceLinks sources={block.sources} />}
                </Fragment>
              )
            )}
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-stone-50 py-16">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6">
      <h2 class="font-heading text-2xl text-brand">Go Deeper on Your First Home Purchase</h2>
      <ul class="mt-6 space-y-4">
        <li>
          <a href="/how-much-house-can-i-afford-idaho" class="font-medium text-gold-dark underline">
            How much house can I afford in Idaho?
          </a>
          <p class="mt-1 text-stone-600">
            How lenders look at income, debt, and credit, and how preapproval works.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="/first-time-buyer-loans-idaho" class="font-medium text-gold-dark underline">
            First-time buyer loans and down payment help in Idaho
          </a>
          <p class="mt-1 text-stone-600">
            Compare conventional, FHA, VA, and USDA loans, plus Idaho Housing down payment assistance.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="/first-time-buyer-areas-southeast-idaho" class="font-medium text-gold-dark underline">
            Where to buy your first home near Idaho Falls
          </a>
          <p class="mt-1 text-stone-600">
            Compare Idaho Falls, Ammon, Rigby, Shelley, Blackfoot, and Rexburg.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="/my-plan" class="font-medium text-gold-dark underline">
            Home buying calculator and readiness checklist
          </a>
          <p class="mt-1 text-stone-600">
            Estimate your monthly payment and see what to do before you buy.
          </p>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-gold/10 py-16">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6">
      <h2 class="font-heading text-2xl text-brand">
        {`Free First-Time Buyer Consultation With ${agent}`}
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-stone-600">
        {agent}, a licensed Idaho real estate agent with {brokerage}, offers first-time buyers a
        free 20 to 30 minute video call on Google Meet. The call covers the buying process, your
        budget, pre-approval, and what to do first. There is no obligation.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-stone-500">
        {agent} is not an attorney or a mortgage lender. For legal questions, ask a real estate
        attorney; for loan options, talk with a mortgage lender.
      </p>
      <a href="/get-started" class="mt-4 inline-block font-medium text-gold-dark">
        Book your free first-time buyer consultation &rarr;
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-brand py-16 text-white">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 text-center">
      <h2 class="font-heading text-2xl">
        {`How ${agent} Helps First-Time Buyers From Pre-Approval to Closing`}
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-stone-200">
        {agent} helps first-time buyers with home search and tours, offers and negotiation, and the
        contract-to-closing process.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-4">
        <a href="/what-i-offer" class="text-sm font-medium text-gold">
          See how Thomas helps first-time buyers &rarr;
        </a>
        <a href="/get-started" class="text-sm font-medium text-gold">
          Book a free buyer consultation &rarr;
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
